    <item>
      <title>Day 3: Patagonia National Park</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/posts/day3/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Mar 2026 23:43:21 -0300</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/posts/day3/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I woke up this morning in a river that overlooked the Rio Baker with the mountains in the backdrop. Not a bad way to start off the day. With some boxed wine and a full dinner last night, I was ready to start my day.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It was a slow morning of having breakfast, playing with the cats and dogs as we all sat out getting our sunshine and starting to warm up. The cats were either scrating up against the tree bark, the kitten wanting to play fight, and all of them alternating between the sun and some shade under by car.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 2: Puerto Rio Tranquillo &amp; Parque Exploradores</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/posts/day2/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Mar 2026 23:43:21 -0300</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/posts/day2/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I woke up at 6:30am this morning to catch my reservation to kayak to Rio Tranquillo&amp;rsquo;s most notable highlight - Marble Caves. It started off a bit misty, but quickly cleared off as the sun rose for sunrise. Luckily it had rained this morning, since it means that the winds don&amp;rsquo;t pick up over the water leaving us with a glassy lake.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;post-image-container&#34; style=&#34;max-width: 1000px; margin: 2rem auto; text-align: center;&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;figure style=&#34;margin: 0;&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;img &#xA;                src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/images/Day2/kayak_outfit_hu_d04fa5eefdb68f8c.png&#34; &#xA;                width=&#34;1000&#34; &#xA;                height=&#34;1332&#34; &#xA;                alt=&#34;These dry suits wrap around the opening of the kayak to keep you totally dry and warm in your normal clothes&#34;&#xA;                style=&#34;max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 4px;&#34;&#xA;            &gt;&#xA;            &#xA;                &lt;figcaption style=&#34;font-size: 0.85rem; color: #666; margin-top: 0.75rem; font-style: italic;&#34;&gt;&#xA;                    These dry suits wrap around the opening of the kayak to keep you totally dry and warm in your normal clothes&#xA;                &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &#xA;        &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;post-image-container&#34; style=&#34;max-width: 1000px; margin: 2rem auto; text-align: center;&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;figure style=&#34;margin: 0;&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;img &#xA;                src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/images/Day2/gerald_on_kayak_hu_9d8f82c6798bc505.png&#34; &#xA;                width=&#34;1000&#34; &#xA;                height=&#34;747&#34; &#xA;                alt=&#34;&#34;&#xA;                style=&#34;max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 4px;&#34;&#xA;            &gt;&#xA;            &#xA;        &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;post-image-container&#34; style=&#34;max-width: 1000px; margin: 2rem auto; text-align: center;&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;figure style=&#34;margin: 0;&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;img &#xA;                src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/images/Day2/kayak_groupphoto_hu_13efedb4d498ef39.png&#34; &#xA;                width=&#34;1000&#34; &#xA;                height=&#34;746&#34; &#xA;                alt=&#34;A fun crew of Chileans, Germans, Americans, and Dutch tourists that made for a funny mix of language interpretations&#34;&#xA;                style=&#34;max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 4px;&#34;&#xA;            &gt;&#xA;            &#xA;                &lt;figcaption style=&#34;font-size: 0.85rem; color: #666; margin-top: 0.75rem; font-style: italic;&#34;&gt;&#xA;                    A fun crew of Chileans, Germans, Americans, and Dutch tourists that made for a funny mix of language interpretations&#xA;                &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;            &#xA;        &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Day 1: Coyhaique to Puerto Rio Tranquillo</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/posts/day1/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 10 Mar 2026 23:43:21 -0300</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/out-of-sandbox/posts/day1/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;After yesterday&amp;rsquo;s travels, I decided to sleep in some more today and enjoy a bit of this quiant Hostel made up of old typewriters, a fireplace, and sliding doors counter-weighted by knitted hens. I hit the road by 8AM to get a headstart on the day since I would have the long drive ahead of me. I grabbed gas at the local Copec Station and began my way down South for Puerto Rio Tranquillo, but had no idea what magic the day had in store for me.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
